  // floor dipping into small lava pools; layer 1 at -430; layer 4 at -706, which is more open and
  // whose floor holds wider lava pools. Lava, the ceiling lights and the eye adaptation are the only
  // light (no skylight reaches this deep); the red fog is LayerClimate's hell tint. Then one spot per
  // hell biome (L-7/L-8): the Ashlands at layer 0 (ash floor, scorched walls, ember crystals), the
  // Magma Caverns at layer 1 (basalt, magma blocks, lava pools) and a Fungal Grove at layer 1 (fungal
  // moss, fungal glow), each looked at ahead, down at the floor and up at the ceiling.
